  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#33\", \"PowerToys#117\", \"PowerToys#11246\"], \"answer\": \"This feature request has been filed before. PowerToys#33 is the main tracking issue for a right-click context menu editor, and PowerToys#117 was closed as a duplicate of it. PowerToys doesn't have this feature yet. The discussion in #33 suggests the work is stalled unless a community member builds it. You can add a +1 or your use case to #33. In the meantime, third-party tools can help. ContextMenuManager edits the old-style menu. NileSoft Shell can remove entries, for example with `remove(find=...)`. ShellExView and ShellMenuView from NirSoft can disable shell extensions that apps left behind. None of these is part of PowerToys, and I haven't tested any of them.\"}",
